// ============================================================================
// Layer rules
// ============================================================================
// Translated from config/hypr/layers.lua (backdrop blur for the Quickshell
// layer surfaces). Under Hyprland this used `layerrule = blur, ignore_alpha`.
//
// niri 26.04 has NO `ignore_alpha` equivalent for forced blur: a layer rule
// with `background-effect { blur true }` blurs the WHOLE rectangle of the
// surface, including its fully transparent areas. The Quickshell panels and
// the app launcher are large, mostly transparent overlay surfaces, so forcing
// blur on them painted a full-height blur sheet over the desktop whenever a
// panel opened.
//
// Fix: do not force blur on the shell's surfaces. niri still blurs any surface
// that requests it through the `ext-background-effect` protocol, and the shell
// keeps its own translucency (settings.json "glass"). If you want a narrow
// glass bar later, re-enable the rule below scoped ONLY to the bar namespace
// (`quickshell`), never to the popup/overlay namespaces.
// ============================================================================

// layer-rule {
//     match namespace="^quickshell$"
//
//     background-effect {
//         blur true
//         xray true
//         saturation 1.1
//     }
// }
